    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bidis</span></b> , is, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in Sicily</i>, <i>north-west of Syracuse</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 22, §
			53</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bidinus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Bidis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palaestritae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 22, § 54</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bi-dini</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Bidis</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 22, § 53</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 8, 14, § 91</span></i>.</div>
